The project is named "SylEnterprise".
Bring in "net" as net.
Bring in "db" as db.
Bring in "time" as time.

Print "Booting Enterprise Server...".

Note: Logs a security event to the console.
Define an action called log_event taking message:
    Print "SEC_LOG: " joined with message.

Connect to database "users.db" as user_db.

Execute query "CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS logins (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, time TEXT);" on user_db.

Listen for HTTP on port 8080.

When a request hits "/login":
    Set current_val to the current date.
    Set query to "INSERT INTO logins (time) VALUES ('" joined with current_val.
    Set query to query joined with "');".
    
    Attempt to Execute query query on user_db.
    
    If it succeeds:
        Reply with "User logged in successfully at " joined with current_val.
    If it fails:
        Reply with "Database Error.".
